{"s13c6b70be42993":"Bread crumbs","s3a78695388b38b":"Home","s8a5edab2826324":"/","s8c6bc099534a02":"Blog","s85184272ec44bd":"Technical articles","s0e91474c2cf971":"2025.07.31","s7df7cd31d7ee5a":"HAMi Heterogeneous Device Virtualization with Hygon DCU: vDCU Resource Scheduling in K8s","s5bf79a6c396636":"Cyclical","s234f1b97e70059":"Dynamia","sd27e8a1e813513":"Editorial team","sff66f1956b6ac7":"Copy article link","sd714f5a8328caf":"HAMi Support for DCU","s434e7cd81fe199":"Technical foundations · Engineering · Open-source insights","sec7580fa3d47ab":"DYNAMIA · OPEN SOURCE & AI INFRASTRUCTURE","s47c24fdafd7fc3":"This is an analysis of how the Hygon DCU device has been able to achieve harmonization through HAMi by completing virtualization.","sca5bfa7775f7cb":"Section 5 of this catalogue","sbae1aff66c2fff":"Catalogue of articles","s938db8c9f82c8c":"01","sf3c3200ac1229c":"vDCU Foundation Operations","sa953f09a1b6b67":"02","s1da1d322955820":"Deployment of HAMi","s0b8efa5a3bf104":"03","s3f80665d35c44c":"Deployment equipment plugins","s6cd5b6e51936a4":"04","s883ab2ec4cdef4":"vDCU Authentication","sc97550ce8213ef":"05","se251641da82450":"Key achievements","s04fb9af7e9edea":"This post is taken from:","s0328142c2be0af":"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/gpyhltXK3CSTkwk4ZwD74A","sa7734a9fe0b0c2":"This was followed by a series of articles analysing the use of HAMi vGPU deployment and the underlying rationale for its realization. The paper analyses how Hygon DCU equipment has been able to achieve harmonization through HAMi completion of virtualization, so as to achieve unified natage and scheduling.","sa5dc53a638e0a9":"1. vDCU-related commands","se9a25e31286541":"Before that, let's just go over how the Hygon DCU's own vDCU functionality is used.","s3825cb933bd0a3":"1.1 View physics DCU resources","sb04ab4f94acef2":"$ hy-smi virtual -show-device-info\n\nDevice 0:\n Actual Device: 0\n Compute units: 60\n Global memory: 34342961152 bytes\nDevice 1:\n Actual Device: 1\n Compute units: 60\n Global memory: 34342961152 bytes\n","s859d75bfddb7de":"1.2 Split vDCU","s5fdacb3e7eb84e":"Disaggregated DCUs 4 containing 5,15,20,20 units and GPU memory of 4096,8192,8192,8192MiB","s547b34e5f79c45":"$ hy-smi virtual -create-vdevices 4 -d 0 \\\n-vdevice-compute-units 5,15,20,20 \\\n-vdevice-memory-size 4096,8192,8192,8192\n\nThe virtual device is created successfully!\n","s487e073f4b1e8e":"1.3 View vdcu information","s3f682e6bc0b769":"$ hy-smi virtual -show-vdevice-info\nVirtual Device 0:\n Actual Device: 7\n Compute units: 5\n Global memory: 4294967296 bytes\n- 5 -\nVirtual Device 1:\n Actual Device: 7\n Compute units: 15\n Global memory: 8589934592 bytes\nVirtual Device 2:\n Actual Device: 7\n Compute units: 20\n Global memory: 8589934592 bytes\nVirtual Device 3:\n Actual Device: 7\n Compute units: 20\n Global memory: 8589934592 bytes\n","s1c1f24f08e3c8b":"1.4 Destruction of vDCU","s8472cda99c0142":"# -d ${dev_id} 指定物理 DCU ID，不指定则选定所有物理 DCU","sc831287e292975":"# -destroy-vdevice 销毁此物理 DCU 上所有 vDCU","sa30ccbb9a66376":"\nhy-smi virtual -d ","sa9ffd96a0601ff":"${dev_id}","s54b3181dddc16c":" -destroy-vdevice\n","s4bf88c765abfcd":"1.5 Docker uses vDCU","s92e4ceb62950ce":"When the container is activated, the following commands are executed to mount vDCU in the container. The following command indicates that when the packaging is activated, the user mounts instance no. vDCU.","sab59659ef78093":"docker run -it --name container_name \\\n--device=/dev/kfd \\\n--device=/dev/dri \\\n--device=/dev/mkfd \\\n-v /etc/vdev/vdev0.conf:/etc/vdev/docker/vdev0.conf:ro \\\n","sb2f3cde5172167":"${docker_image:tag}","s2b5eab8a02e74b":" \\\n/bin/bash\n","sde2c27e3da9a87":"It can be seen that an additional document/etc/vdev/vdev0.conf is mounted in the container, in addition to the equipment files such as kfd, dri, mkfd, which are mounted by --device.","sd2561bed93ae3b":"This file is actually a profile of the vDCU, which is internally recorded.","s9917d1ebd3489a":"Although the relevant source code is not available, it is certain that the driver will see whether the file exists or, if so, indicate that VDCU is currently used and then find corresponding physical DCUs based on the information in the document, as well as core, mem etc. to complete the restriction.","s94db36584e80d6":"Look next at how the HAMi uses vDCU.","s7b0a23af2e29f6":"2. Deployment of HAMi","s899404e1a3ed49":"Preconditions:","sbe49230de2c046":"dtk driver > = 24.04","s8a128fec461be4":"2.1 Deployment","s70a910570dfbfb":"Deployment with Helm","s8a96e0a972a089":"# 添加 repo","sa4074e6b6a640c":"\nhelm repo add hami-charts https://project-hami.github.io/HAMi/\n","se678db8e5fd085":"# 安装","sa83224eae8ca3b":"\nhelm install hami hami-charts/hami -n kube-system\n","s81d4f9b13eafda":"ps: can be adjusted ","s035258a9b5c9ad":"HAMi Deployment Configuration","se83868de5e872c":"It's from defining your installation.","s8139dc2af273d1":"If the current environment is not able to access an online mirror, you can specify a mirror repository.","sd46aee08cc49f6":"export","sc9fc092cfd4a35":" registry=192.168.10.172:5000\n","s86c4a2c81f6d76":"# 不指定 tag,会自动使用当前集群同样版本，需要确保 Registry 有该镜像","s8f687b10130f1a":" kubescheduler=","s272f343aa29a03":"$registry","s614cc4e13464f7":"/kube-scheduler\n\nhelm upgrade --install hami hami-charts/hami -n kube-system \\\n--","s6ee0eb490ff832":"set","sbfdb6565ff5fde":" scheduler.kubeScheduler.image=","secef426937e657":"$kubescheduler","s8112ea4bfca676":" \\\n--","sc542318bf9187b":" scheduler.extender.image=","s73106724f7e9c2":"/projecthami/hami \\\n--","s612258428bd20b":" scheduler.patch.imageNew=","s3a7fa6277b7f31":"/liangjw/kube-webhook-certgen:v1.1.1\n","s282d1a8f52aff2":"2.2 Inspection of Pod operations","s37ba5975058c44":"$ kubectl -n kube-system get po -l app.kubernetes.io/name=hami\nNAME                              READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\nhami-scheduler-6dbdf69644-mz9m5   2/2     Running   0          2m19s\n","s1fb3caae369b7e":"If hami-scheduler Running indicates successful installation.","sfde2d75d56c910":"ps: For the DCU environment only start a family-scheduler Pod.","s0cb5a1e2011c18":"3. Deployment of hami-vdcu-device-plugin","sfcb3ff47b3c14d":"# 对应的 DevicePlugin 也是用 HAMi 社区提供的版本。","sf29b84f6aacc44":"# 先给 DCU 节点打上 label dcu=on","s8e23fd6665a66c":"\nkubectl label nodes {nodeid} dcu=on\n","s98e5f6a83f4c2f":"3.1 Preparatory work","sf47cd02f8d669e":"And then we'll do the following preparatory work.","se9abda2b57d5e0":"Create vdev directory","sf91eaedfd858e8":"# on the dcu node, create these directory:","s493a4db2c28a55":"\n$ ","s95c5007a9af81a":"mkdir","s2af2272b93cc4a":" /etc/vdev\n","s03c472a3519b1a":"Copy dtk to /opt/dtk directory","s08859dc2a9b1cd":"Because the container will be mounted in a uniform manner, it will be moved from the deployment catalogue cp to the specified directory","s652dbf692b871a":"# should change dtk-xx.xx.x to your installed dtk version","se44b4bd707c540":"cp","s09b55e3cece6b3":" -r /opt/dtk-xx.xx.x /opt/dtk\n","sf6cbdc4d3b3626":"Note: /opt/dtk-xx.xx.x This position depends on the directory specified when DTK is previously deployed","se97c2d1f8814d2":"3.2 Deployment","sce64f4a9174d09":"Then we can begin to deploy.","se484a95dcc8586":"From ","sfc80caf86c8a69":"https://github.com/Project-HAMi/dcu-vgpu-device-plugin","s8c8791657c643d":" Project acquisition related","saae698234c8189":"wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Project-HAMi/dcu-vgpu-device-plugin/refs/heads/master/k8s-dcu-plugin.yaml\nwget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Project-HAMi/dcu-vgpu-device-plugin/refs/heads/master/k8s-dcu-rbac.yaml\n","sdd011c5bd99bde":"Then deploy device-plugin","s00b5a1b4f546f1":"kubectl apply -f k8s-dcu-rbac.yaml\nkubectl apply -f k8s-dcu-plugin.yaml\n","sbc25e3661df930":"3.3 Inspection of Pod operations","se11029a7f18972":"Confirm that the components are functioning:","sd8153e0d7baa40":"$ kubectl get po -n kube-code\nNAMESPACE     NAME                                      READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\nkube-code     hami-dcu-vgpu-device-plugin-cgwwv        1/1     Running   4          14m\nkube-code     hami-dcu-vgpu-device-plugin-lp7gl        1/1     Running   0          8m36s\nkube-code     hami-dcu-vgpu-device-plugin-lswbl        1/1     Running   0          8m40s\nkube-code     hami-dcu-vgpu-device-plugin-svwl7        1/1     Running   0          8m38s\nkube-code     hami-scheduler-bb5586989-q7bvr           2/2     Running   0          54m\n","s6f72ed5d26de00":"As you can see, the dcu-vdcu-device-plugin on several DCU nodes is functioning normally.","s846c44b20ea3b6":"So, the components are deployed and the vDCU is then verified for normal use.","sc725a7ca9205d7":"4. Validation vdcu","s6471a2cfd42aa2":"4.1 View Node resources","s73d497c495e22e":"Next is to see if the node resources are properly registered.","s686fab4e8edc6e":"$ kubectl describe node d41gpucns41 | grep Capacity -A 8  \nCapacity:\n  cpu:                64\n  ephemeral-storage:  934609028Ki\n  hugepages-1Gi:      0\n  hugepages-2Mi:      0\n  hygon.com/dcu:      0\n  hygon.com/dcunum:   32\n  memory:             1043017856Ki\n  pods:               500\n","s40191fae12258b":"Here's the hygon.com/dcunum: 32 is the vdcu number, single node 8 DCU, and here it's four times split.","se258d3895e4076":"ps: Because the current piece of Hygon Physics DCU supports only the division of four vDCUs.","se61654dffb1910":"4.2 Start Pod with vdcu","sea1e8e161b97eb":"Full yaml is as follows:","s111d0e0c3c7afe":"apiVersion:","s3bfc269594ef64":"v1","s08863725c9d14a":"kind:","s0a6bb8b01de101":"Pod","s8c8c42289a1387":"metadata:","sd0d6d503f5acae":"name:","s2562e8738c499d":"alexnet-tf-gpu-pod-mem","sfa1e8330316fdd":"labels:","s6c7fc2130847a7":"purpose:","s115bd458691017":"demo-tf-amdgpu","s36184fa5172f39":"spec:","s04968f51ee0482":"containers:","s3973e022e93220":"-","s2e94c3d77b445f":"alexnet-tf-gpu-container","sa08a30338e824c":"image:","sd9ed447f601a42":"ubuntu:20.04","sae773d9b560702":"workingDir:","s94a6b447580330":"/root","s8ff7327fcdf50a":"command:","sc4ebc7684be8c9":" [","s0bb2388cc80f97":"\"sleep\"","s0a07f659461970":", ","s016ae398a67dbf":"\"infinity\"","s30348c92376d56":"]\n      ","scab2be2b3a2ed1":"resources:","s2629ac0e8d90da":"limits:","s83389c3b91ab78":"hygon.com/dcunum:","s6b86b273ff34fc":"1","s1d1aba1613848f":"# requesting a GPU","s54061bce2ee740":"hygon.com/dcumem:","s81a83544cf93c2":"2000","s74788a0708c6f9":"# each dcu require 2000 MiB device memory","s1e76f0d86a1472":"hygon.com/dcucores:","se629fa6598d732":"15","s8a6181c6cdcc5d":"# each dcu use 15% of total compute cores","sb02687304956a5":"Similar to vGPU, support the designation of separate card numbers, core, mem etc.","s2fcc3cf5606fde":"Enter Pod before source environment variable","s41cf6794ba4200":"source","s4c1e40a552d992":" /opt/hygondriver/env.sh\n","sf549d2e055491a":"Then you can use the following command to verify it.","s6c14b6f61ba02f":"hy-virtual -show-device-info\n","s0a3aabd969b702":"Device 0:\n        Actual Device: 0\n        Compute units: 9\n        Global memory: 2097152000 bytes\n","s65038df1c20212":"Compute units and Global memory are the cores and mems that we've identified before.","sb08d3beb49ea74":"So, the description of HAMi vdcu is already in effect.","s7db44c0ecabb8f":"4.3 Attention","s4b080fa717ae7d":"Some notes:","sa18c1db654b7e0":"If your mirror is not 'dtk-embedded-image', you will need to install pciutiils, libelf-dev, kmod after the job is run, otherwise a dcu tool like hy-smi or hy-virtual may not work properly.","s6368ee5df85121":"The sharing of DCUs, init containers with \"hygon.com/dcumm\" pop will not be supported in the init container and will never be scheduling.","s782913a1a51fb8":"Only one vdcu can be obtained for each container. If you want to mount more than one dcc device, no hygon.com/dcum or hygon.com/dcucores should be set.","s38411d81221766":"5. Realization analysis","sb42d0451d0941e":"A brief analysis of vdcu-device-plugin, available from the steps using vDCU in chapter I, vdcu-device-plugin","s007a1aa5698f15":"In addition to normal information on the equipment being reported and distributed, the following matters need to be addressed:","s97520261d927e6":"vDCU profile maintenance","sa12b18ebc59076":"Generate the corresponding vdcu profile when creating Pod based on core, mem in yaml","sf51ce4641eaaec":"Pod also needs to delete the corresponding profile after it is deleted","s1d6454a3a84100":"Mounting vDCU profile to Pod","sc84bc4fb51be1b":"Only then will the driver know how much to limit the vDCU to.","s134e5c524b55a1":"I suggest you read this first.","se48340b00e488e":"Part 1: Analysis of the rationale for the HAMi vGPU programme","s52b4aededa3004":"It is similar to that.","s2c81226f7b6e50":"5.1 Register","sef2bde6f268ea8":"The first is to register DevicePlugin in Kubelet, which uses the data-plugin-manager so there's no code for separate registration, but it's also possible to see what was done on startup.","s43b6add39a6dd7":"// Start is an optional interface that could be implemented by plugin.","se0a972b06d317f":"// If case Start is implemented, it will be executed by Manager after","s21cbc8e8bae51e":"// plugin instantiation and before its registration to kubelet. This","s58e20cb97c0025":"// method could be used to prepare resources before they are offered","s2824a50b07e5c4":"// to Kubernetes.","sf63827270b1643":"func","se77fb3d05dd2e7":"(p *Plugin)","s2c850805f1da8a":" Start() ","sca00fccfb40898":"error","s5dc13be20915e0":" {\n   ","sc86872dc97dd35":"var","s22522af15b77e7":" err ","s8c48f7421a99b5":"// 初始化 device info","sdc63b820a2cc6b":"\n   dcgm.Init()\n   p.devices, err = dcgm.DeviceInfos()\n   ","s935f68319d4f22":"if","sa12f6fa7b5ccdc":" err != ","s5da3a4c7f11794":"nil","sc4ef01f1ae3730":" {\n       log.Fatalf(","s2eebe3dfbd801a":"\"dcgm DeviceInfos failed:%s\"","se1cffd645f63a5":", err.Error())\n   }\n   ","s10c22bcf4c768b":"for","s70d06600df27d9":" idx := ","s2269c0be009b61":"range","s87f666b3c51977":" p.devices {\